description:
[narrowed from orphaned-capability-scan-test-asserts-on-captured-reads-not-writes] repos/development-vessel/test/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.test.ts asserts on emission by position and by raw count, but its harness captures every call the resolver makes, reads included. Five of its six tests fail as a result. The resolver is correct and must not be changed.

wireSubstrate's third route captures EVERY POST to /v2/impulses/resolve. The resolver writes its gap as substrateGap_write but also reads substrateGap twice, so emits[0] is a read, not the write.

Make these four edits, all in test/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.test.ts. Do not touch src/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.ts.

EDIT 1 — replace this exact line:

    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.type).toBe("substrateGap_write");

with these two lines:

    const _w = emits.filter((e: any) => e.impulse.pointer.type === "substrateGap_write");
    expect(_w.length).toBe(1);

EDIT 2 — in the same test, replace these two exact lines:

    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.gap.category).toBe("orphaned_capability");
    expect(emits[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe("orphaned-capability-problem_detection");

with:

    expect(_w[0].impulse.pointer.gap.category).toBe("orphaned_capability");
    expect(_w[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe("orphaned-capability-problem_detection");

EDIT 3 — this exact line occurs three times (at roughly lines 80, 110 and 120). Replace EVERY occurrence:

    expect(emits.length).toBe(0);

with:

    expect(emits.filter((e: any) => e.impulse.pointer.type === "substrateGap_write").length).toBe(0);

EDIT 4 — replace this exact line:

    expect(a[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe(b[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id);

with:

    const _wa = a.filter((e: any) => e.impulse.pointer.type === "substrateGap_write");
    const _wb = b.filter((e: any) => e.impulse.pointer.type === "substrateGap_write");
    expect(_wa[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id).toBe(_wb[0].impulse.pointer.gap.id);

Change nothing else. Leave wireSubstrate, TEMPLATES, the resolver import, and every other assertion exactly as they are.

Why this is correct: the resolver's behaviour is already right — body.gaps_emitted is 1 in the first test and that assertion already passes, so exactly one write occurs. The tests were measuring captured reads as if they were emissions.

ORACLE: test/resolvers/orphaned-capability-scan.test.ts goes from 1 pass / 5 fail to 6 pass / 0 fail. I applied exactly these four edits to a scratch copy and confirmed 6 pass / 0 fail, so this target is known reachable.

The file must typecheck. This vessel carries a standing baseline of pre-existing failures elsewhere — judge on newly-failing tests, not absolute counts.

